            "paragraph": "Most commonly, the damage function is assumed to take the form: \u03c0 = (\u03c6\u0394T^2)/(1+\u03c6\u0394T^2) (4). A quadratic function is a simplification that has been hotly debated as it appears to exclude the potential for catastrophic economic damages that might arise from tipping points in the climate system and that might introduce a higher order temperature dependency (Burke et al., 2015; Dietz et al., 2021; Keen et al., 2022).",
            "ontology_conformed": false,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
